# Normalise line endings so a Linux CI runner and a Windows dev machine agree.
#
# eol=lf is the load-bearing half. .editorconfig pins end_of_line = lf for C#, and
# dotnet format enforces it against the WORKING TREE, not against what git stores.
# Plain 'text=auto' normalises to LF in the repository but hands each platform its
# native ending on checkout - so a Windows checkout got CRLF and dotnet format
# reported every line of every C# file as wrong, on main as much as on a branch.
# That buried real findings under dozens of false ones. eol=lf makes the checkout
# match the formatter everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.cs        text diff=csharp
*.razor     text
*.csproj    text
*.props     text
*.slnx      text
*.md        text
*.json      text
*.config    text
*.yml       text
*.ps1       text
# LF always: CI runs this on ubuntu and git bash chokes on a CRLF shebang line.
*.sh        text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
